        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix stack-safe large attachment handling",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses #90098.\n\nThis branch is now rebased onto current OpenClaw architecture and deliberately narrowed to the parts still missing from `main`:\n\n- replace the gateway's full-payload data-URL capture regex with bounded index/slice parsing;\n- replace the Control UI send-path data-URL capture regex in `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.ts`;\n- replace the pasted-image full-payload regex in `ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-composer.ts` with a bounded header check plus iterative payload validation;\n- discard stale failed composer queue entries created by the old `Maximum call stack size exceeded` failure;\n- add focused gateway and current-UI regression coverage.\n\nCurrent `main` already contains iterative base64 validation and the broader 20 MB / 20-page inbound extraction policy, so this update keeps those upstream implementations and drops the obsolete extraction-limit/config churn from the older branch.\n\n## What problem this solves\n\nMulti-megabyte PDF/image data URLs were still passed through regexes that captured the entire base64 payload. On sufficiently large browser or gateway sends, V8 could throw `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` before the attachment reached normal validation/offload handling. Failed Control UI sends carrying that historical error could also be restored and replayed after upgrade.\n\nThe new parsing keeps regex use bounded to a short MIME header and processes the payload by index/iteration.\n\n## Current changed paths\n\n- `src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts`\n- `src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-composer.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/composer-persistence.ts`\n- `ui/src/pages/chat/composer-persistence.test.ts`\n\n## Verification\n\nRegression coverage on the current file layout now includes:\n\n- a 12 MiB gateway data URL parsed/offloaded without a full-payload regex;\n- a large Control UI attachment serialized through `chat.send`;\n- a large pasted image converted through the current composer;\n- rejection of invalid pasted base64;\n- identifiable pre-fix attachment stack-overflow records dropped during restore, while current failures and unrelated text failures with the same generic V8 phrase remain durable and retryable via a stored item-format marker.\n\nFresh GitHub CI is running on exact head `9beef8b734634b0c96b2511ad821ab09e7fc572a`, which contains the shared upstream cutoff `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e` and the narrowed legacy-cleanup repair.\n\nAdditional exact-head repair validation: 281 focused Control UI tests pass across composer persistence, chat state, and chat send; formatting, targeted oxlint, and diff checks also pass. The storage-only marker is retained across internal normalization only for affected failed attachment records and is stripped from public queue snapshots.\n\n## Real behavior evidence\n\nThe original branch was validated with a real Chrome upload of a 9.18 MB, 8-page PDF (roughly a 12 MB base64 data URL) against a live gateway. The upload completed without `RangeError`, was offloaded, and the model received extracted page content. That live run was on the pre-port head; this update ports the same stack-safe parsing behavior to today's gateway and UI paths and adds exact-path regression tests. No new live Signal/provider/device claim is being made for this merge-only port.\n\nGenerated with AI assistance; all security-sensitive parsing remains fail-closed for malformed payloads.\n",
        "branch": "fix/90098-canonical-media-limits",
